  "summary": "I love to start my days with coffee and code! I am an entry level software engineer with three years of experience through college. Even though I am an entry level developer, I strive to find the best possible solution and learn along the way. I have been promoted several times at my current job because of my abilities to adapt and learn quick. I am looking to expand my knowledge and soak up as much information as I can along my journey.\n\nWHAT I BRING:\nI bring to the table entry level knowledge on C#, SQL Server, .NET, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and more. I am consistently learning and up for any challenge that comes my way. I can use Visual studio, Azure, and more. I love to sit down with tasks and I wont stop until I complete each one. If I do not know something I am not afraid to ask questions and do my research to figure out what I need. I bring a positive mindset and a joyful young developer to any project I get assigned to. \n\nGOALS:\nMy  long term goal is to find a company that suits me and will give me the opportunity to learn and grow as a developer. My 5 year plan is to be working for a great company that allows my to be myself and to be proficient in whatever languages I need to build the best solutions possible.\n\nSPECIALITIES: \nC#, HTML/CSS/Javascript, full stack, .NET, Xamarin",
